# A Meta Quest plugged in by USB (or plugged in already at login) starts Prostir for the
# user's session, where Prostir waits for the headset (prostir.socket is on; otherwise
# prostir.service does not start): it sets up `adb reverse`, so the headset reaches it
# through USB. Not on `add` only: a later `bind` or `change` event would drop what
# `add` set, and a user's systemd that starts after it (at login) would see none.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="2833", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="prostir.service"
